Input: {"question": "Who produced the album \"The Athens Demos\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d00", "start": 0, "end": 189, "text": "Fables of the Reconstruction Fables of the Reconstruction, also known as Reconstruction of the Fables, is the third studio album by American alternative rock band R.E.M., released on I.R.S."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d00", "start": 190, "end": 206, "text": "Records in 1985."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d00", "start": 207, "end": 297, "text": "The Joe Boyd-produced album was the first recorded by the group outside the United States."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d00", "start": 298, "end": 363, "text": "It is a concept album with Southern Gothic themes and characters."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d00", "start": 364, "end": 498, "text": "Despite the growing audience and critical acclaim experienced by the band after its first two albums, \"Murmur\" and \"Reckoning\", R.E.M."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d00", "start": 499, "end": 624, "text": "decided to make noticeable changes to its style of music and recording habits, including a change in producer to Joe Boyd and"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d01", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": "Seven Seas ” ?"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d01", "start": 15, "end": 60, "text": "What ’ s Inside the Pyramid at Chichén Itzá ?"}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d01", "start": 61, "end": 212, "text": "The 10 Greatest Basketball Players of All Time Titanosaurs : 8 of the World 's Biggest Dinosaurs Contents Fables of the Reconstruction album by R.E.M ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d01", "start": 213, "end": 343, "text": "Ask the Chatbot a Question Ask the Chatbot a Question Learn about this topic in these articles : discussed in biography In R.E.M ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d01", "start": 344, "end": 431, "text": "…was the band ’ s 1985 release , Fables of the Reconstruction , a tense blend of R.E.M."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d01", "start": 432, "end": 518, "text": "’ s ideas about folk rock and those of Joe Boyd , an American expatriate who worked in"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "start": 0, "end": 8, "text": "In time."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "start": 9, "end": 94, "text": "Chris Jones 2008 Three albums into their career and R.E.M were about to hit a crisis."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "start": 95, "end": 199, "text": "As with many bands, a lot of their new material was gleaned from a world-view shaped by endless touring."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "start": 200, "end": 232, "text": "Such is the lot of a young band."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "start": 233, "end": 324, "text": "The American landscape seeps into both Stipe's lyrics and the band's jangly, electric folk."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "start": 325, "end": 416, "text": "With this in mind, it must have made perfect sense to enlist the help of hip-hop mogul, Dr."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "start": 417, "end": 529, "text": "Dre; the man who produced classics by various artists, bringing his unique production style to the band's sound."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "start": 530, "end": 533, "text": "Dr."}, "D3S9": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "start": 534, "end": 671, "text": "Dre's influence can be heard in the raw, gritty feel of \"The Athens Demos,\" which marked a significant departure from their earlier work."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d03", "start": 0, "end": 245, "text": "Here `` Released : June 1985 `` Driver 8 `` Released : September 1985 `` Wendell Gee `` Released : September 1985 Fables of the Reconstruction ( or Reconstruction of the Fables ) is the third studio album by American alternative rock band R.E.M."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d03", "start": 246, "end": 294, "text": "It was released on June 10, 1985, through I.R.S."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d03", "start": 295, "end": 303, "text": "Records."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d03", "start": 304, "end": 448, "text": "It was the band's first album recorded outside of the U.S., with sessions taking place at Livingston Studios in London with producer Elton John."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d03", "start": 449, "end": 528, "text": "The record displays a darker, murkier sound than its predecessors, with lyrics."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d04", "start": 0, "end": 254, "text": "titles to denote the two sides , while CD releases use the Reconstruction title on the spine and the Fables title on the disc , with the liner notes featuring a reversible cover ( based on the back cover of the LP release ) themed around the two titles ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d04", "start": 255, "end": 375, "text": "Face on the Cover : Headshots of all four band members , illuminated by slide projections , feature on the front cover ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d04", "start": 376, "end": 478, "text": "The Gilded Age : The American Reconstruction is alluded to in the Fables of the Reconstruction title ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d04", "start": 479, "end": 539, "text": "Idiosyncratic Episode Naming : LP and cassette copies divide"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0067-297ecd682aa6:d02:c0", "entity": "album producer", "scope": "The Athens Demos album", "claim": "Dr. Dre produced the album \"The Athens Demos\".", "answer": "Dr. Dre", "quote": "Dre; the man who produced classics by various artists, bringing his unique production style to the band's sound. Dr. Dre's influence can be heard in the raw, gritty feel of \"The Athens Demos,\" which marked a significant departure from their earlier work.", "original_document_number": 3}], "current_answers": ["Dr. Dre", "Joe Boyd", "Elton John"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Dr. Dre", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Joe Boyd", "origin": "coverage_addition"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "Elton John", "origin": "coverage_addition"}], "requested_slot_hint": "person"}
